{"seq":4,"slug":"major-works","title":"庄子·major-works","stage":"DONE","category":"zhuangzi","categoryLabel":"庄子","chapterCount":3,"docCount":6,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works","rating":{"composite":3.57,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.4,"coverage":3,"positioning":4,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/famous-people/25_zhuangzi/4_major-works","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"庄子-主要著作\">庄子·主要著作</h1><p>《庄子》既是哲学经典，又是文学杰作。本 hub 不讲庄子的<strong>思想内容</strong>（那属姊妹 hub），而专注于《庄子》一书的<strong>文本形态与表达艺术</strong>：它由哪些篇章构成、用什么独特方式说理、对语言本身有何反思。换言之，本 hub 的主角是「文本」，而非「义理」。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本-hub-与兄弟-hub-的分工\">本 hub 与兄弟 hub 的分工</h2><p>庄子是个「6 facet」人物 hub。各 facet 分工明确，本 hub 居「作品/文本」之位：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>兄弟 hub</th>\n<th>关注点</th>\n<th>与本 hub 的边界</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><a href=\"../life-and-times/the-warring-states-era/an-age-of-chaos\">生平与时代</a></td>\n<td>庄周其人、战国乱世</td>\n<td>本 hub 不讲生平，只在解释文体动因时引用</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../core-contributions/the-zhuangzi-text/inner-outer-miscellaneous\">核心贡献</a></td>\n<td>文本作为「贡献」的定位</td>\n<td>本 hub 是对其文本部分的<strong>深化细读</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../ideas-and-methods/free-and-easy-wandering/absolute-freedom\">思想与方法</a></td>\n<td>逍遥·齐物·顺自然的<strong>义理</strong></td>\n<td>本 hub 只索引义理、不展开；专讲承载义理的文本与文体</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../influence-and-legacy/shaping-chinese-culture/laozhuang-and-daoism\">影响与遗产</a></td>\n<td>对文化·禅宗·世界的影响</td>\n<td>本 hub 的文体/语言艺术是其影响之<strong>源</strong>，影响之<strong>果</strong>在彼</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../controversies-and-appraisal/questions-of-authorship/the-authorship-question\">争议与评价</a></td>\n<td>著作权、诠释、相对主义之争</td>\n<td>本 hub 引其结论（如内篇可靠性、相对主义争议）作论据</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>一言以蔽：<strong>思想 hub 问「庄子说了什么」，本 hub 问「庄子怎样说、用什么文本说、为何这样说」。</strong></p>\n<h2 id=\"三个子主题与推荐学习路径\">三个子主题与推荐学习路径</h2><p>本 hub 含三个子主题、六篇文档。建议循「文本→寓言→语言」的次序由实入虚：</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"flowchart\" data-source=\"flowchart LR&#10;    A[&quot;1 内篇&lt;br/&gt;(文本骨架)&quot;] --&gt; B[&quot;2 寓言&lt;br/&gt;(说理方式)&quot;]&#10;    B --&gt; C[&quot;3 语言与吊诡&lt;br/&gt;(语言反思)&quot;]\">flowchart LR\n    A[\"1 内篇&lt;br/&gt;(文本骨架)\"] --&gt; B[\"2 寓言&lt;br/&gt;(说理方式)\"]\n    B --&gt; C[\"3 语言与吊诡&lt;br/&gt;(语言反思)\"]</pre><ol>\n<li><strong>内篇七篇</strong>——先建立文本地图。<ul>\n<li><a href=\"the-inner-chapters/the-seven-inner-chapters\">内篇七篇</a>：三十三篇的分卷、七篇主题与体系、内篇可靠性论证。</li>\n<li><a href=\"the-inner-chapters/key-parables\">关键寓言</a>：鲲鹏、庄周梦蝶、浑沌凿窍三则纲领性寓言细读。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>寓言与寓意</strong>——再看庄子如何「以故事说理」。<ul>\n<li><a href=\"fables-and-allegories/teaching-through-stories\">以故事说理</a>：三言体例、形象—抽象耦合机制、独特哲学文体的影响。</li>\n<li><a href=\"fables-and-allegories/cook-ding-and-others\">庖丁解牛与濠梁观鱼</a>：两则跨篇名寓言的文本细读与正反对读。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>语言与吊诡</strong>——终于触及庄子对语言本身的反思。<ul>\n<li><a href=\"language-and-paradox/goblet-words\">卮言与得意忘言</a>：庄子的正面语言策略（如何说、如何读）。</li>\n<li><a href=\"language-and-paradox/the-limits-of-language\">语言的局限与吊诡玄思</a>：语言局限的形上根据与吊诡思维。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>前置知识</strong>：阅读本 hub 前，最好先读 <a href=\"../ideas-and-methods/free-and-easy-wandering/absolute-freedom\">思想与方法 hub</a> 中逍遥、齐物、顺自然三个核心概念——本 hub 的寓言与文本皆围绕这些义理而生，知其义理方能见文本之妙。</p>\n<h2 id=\"阅读本-hub-的一个提醒\">阅读本 hub 的一个提醒</h2><p>《庄子》的文本不能用读论说文的方式读。它「寓言十九」、充满吊诡、主张「得意忘言」——若执着于「找命题、建体系」，必处处觉其自相矛盾。本 hub 各篇反复强调的一个反模式即：<strong>勿望文生义、勿以形式逻辑证伪吊诡之言、勿把虚构寓言当史实</strong>。带着这层自觉读，方能领会庄子「文体即哲学」的深意。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-inner-chapters","title":"The Inner Chapters","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/the-inner-chapters","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-seven-inner-chapters","title":"内篇七篇","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/the-inner-chapters/the-seven-inner-chapters"},{"seq":2,"slug":"key-parables","title":"关键寓言","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/the-inner-chapters/key-parables"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"fables-and-allegories","title":"Fables And Allegories","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/fables-and-allegories","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"teaching-through-stories","title":"以故事说理","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/fables-and-allegories/teaching-through-stories"},{"seq":2,"slug":"cook-ding-and-others","title":"庖丁解牛与濠梁观鱼","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/fables-and-allegories/cook-ding-and-others"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"language-and-paradox","title":"Language And Paradox","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/language-and-paradox","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"goblet-words","title":"卮言与得意忘言","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/language-and-paradox/goblet-words"},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-limits-of-language","title":"语言的局限与吊诡玄思","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/major-works/language-and-paradox/the-limits-of-language"}]}]}